    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d71">

                <pb facs="0179" n="91" sameAs="frus:frus1892/pg91"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Denby to Mr. Blaine.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-03-05"><hi rendition="#italic">March 5, 1892</hi></date>.
                        (Received, April 18.)</dateline><seg rendition="#float-left">No.
                        1485].</seg></opener>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">legation of the united
                        states.</hi></p>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose herewith a
                    translation of a communication from the foreign office on the subject of the
                    action taken by the Government relative to the riot at Wuku last year. The yamên
                    sets out that two of the rioters were arrested and decapitated on the spot.
                    Others were punished by imprisonment and the cargue. Later, another leader, Kao
                    Yu Ching, was arrested and beheaded. Thus the leading criminals have been
                    punished as a warning to others in the future.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Denby.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d71-a1.xml" xpointer="d71-a1"/>
            </div>
